  "rules": "- Normal Sudoku Rules: Fill each row, column, and 3x3 box with the digits 1-9 once each.\n\n- Global entropy: Every 2x2 square of cells must contain a low digit (1,2,3), middle digit (4,5,6) and high digit (7,8,9).\n\n- Global Modularity: Every 2x2 box must contain at least one digit from each of the sets {1,4,7}, {2,5,8} and {3,6,9}.\n\n- Killer Cages: Digits in cages must not repeat and must sum to the number in the upper left corner of the cage (if present).",
